WEBVTT

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:05.000
<v Jane Adviser>Thanks for joining, Gali. How are things since our last review?</v>

00:00:05.500 --> 00:00:12.000
<v Gali Client>Good, thanks. We wanted to talk about increasing our super contributions before the end of the financial year.</v>

00:00:12.500 --> 00:00:22.000
<v Jane Adviser>Sure. Given your risk tolerance, I'd suggest we look at salary sacrificing an extra 5000 dollars and reviewing the balanced growth fund allocation.</v>

00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:30.000
<v Gali Client>That works for us. Can we also book a follow-up review in three months to check progress?</v>

00:00:30.500 --> 00:00:40.000
<v Jane Adviser>Absolutely, I'll send a calendar invite for late October. I'll also email you the updated strategy document with the contribution numbers by Friday.</v>

00:00:40.500 --> 00:00:48.000
<v Gali Client>One flag — we're not sure yet if we'll sell the investment property this year, so hold off finalising the cash flow plan until we confirm.</v>

00:00:48.500 --> 00:00:52.000
<v Jane Adviser>Noted, I'll mark that as pending and follow up once you've decided.</v>

00:00:52.500 --> 00:01:03.000
<v Jane Adviser>While we're on contributions — you're currently at about 14,000 dollars concessional this financial year. The cap is 30,000, so the extra 5,000 salary sacrifice still leaves headroom if you want to use carry-forward amounts from prior years.</v>

00:01:03.500 --> 00:01:11.000
<v Gali Client>I didn't realise we had carry-forward room. How much are we talking about?</v>

00:01:11.500 --> 00:01:24.000
<v Jane Adviser>I'd need to pull your last three years of contribution history to give you an exact figure, so I don't want to quote a number today. I'll check the ATO portal and confirm the carry-forward balance in the strategy document I send you.</v>

00:01:24.500 --> 00:01:31.000
<v Gali Client>Okay, no rush, just flag it in the document. What about the balanced growth fund — is that still the right mix given markets right now?</v>

00:01:31.500 --> 00:01:45.000
<v Jane Adviser>Your allocation is currently 70 growth, 30 defensive, which matches the risk profile from your last questionnaire. I'm not recommending a change today, but we should redo the risk questionnaire at the next review since it's been over two years.</v>

00:01:45.500 --> 00:01:52.000
<v Gali Client>Fair enough. Let's also talk insurance — I think our income protection policy is still through my old employer's group cover.</v>

00:01:52.500 --> 00:02:05.000
<v Jane Adviser>That's worth checking properly rather than me guessing. Group cover often drops away or changes terms when you leave an employer, so can you send me the policy documents, or the insurer's name at least, before our next meeting?</v>

00:02:05.500 --> 00:02:10.000
<v Gali Client>Yes, I'll dig those out this week and send them through.</v>

00:02:10.500 --> 00:02:20.000
<v Jane Adviser>Great, once I have that I'll review the cover level against your current income and let you know if there's a gap. I won't make any recommendation until I've actually seen the policy.</v>

00:02:20.500 --> 00:02:29.000
<v Gali Client>Understood. One more thing — my sister mentioned we should have an updated will since the kids were born. Is that something you help with?</v>

00:02:29.500 --> 00:02:40.000
<v Jane Adviser>We don't draft wills ourselves, but I can refer you to an estate planning solicitor we work with regularly. I'll include their contact details in the follow-up email alongside the strategy document.</v>

00:02:40.500 --> 00:02:47.000
<v Gali Client>That'd be great, thank you. So to confirm — next review in three months, late October?</v>

00:02:47.500 --> 00:02:58.000
<v Jane Adviser>Yes, I'll lock in late October for the full review, and separately I'll follow up with you in about two weeks just to check whether you've decided on the investment property and to collect the insurance policy details.</v>

00:02:58.500 --> 00:03:04.000
<v Gali Client>Sounds good. Thanks Jane, appreciate you covering all of that today.</v>

00:03:04.500 --> 00:03:08.000
<v Jane Adviser>No problem at all, Gali. Speak soon.</v>
